. Algorithm 

1. Start with an empty tree. Every new node has lthread = rthread = true. 
2. Read n and the n values. Insert each value by BST rules. A new node inherits its parent's 
   old thread, and the parent's link becomes a real child link. Duplicates are rejected. 
3. Display the inorder traversal by starting at the leftmost node and repeatedly taking the successor. 
4. Read q, the number of nodes to query, then read the q node values. 
5. For each query value x:
   – Search for x in the tree.
   – If x is not found, print NOT FOUND and go to the next query.
   – If rthread of x is true, the successor is its right link. Mark the link type as THREAD.
   – Otherwise, move to the right child and keep going left until lthread is true.  
   - That node is the successor. Mark the link type as CHILD LINK.
   – If the successor is NULL, print NO inorder successor.
   – Otherwise, print the successor and the link type. 
6.  After all queries are processed, free the tree and stop. Complexity: each successor query takes O(h) 
    time, where h is the height of the tree, and needs no extra stack space.

